    "created_at": "2025-07-28T15:18:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-07-28T15:24:07Z",
    "body": "CSS Color 4 says\n\n> Values must be [rounded towards +∞](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values-4/#combine-integers), not truncated\n\nFrom my pov the important part is round not truncate (which has been a source of poor interop in the past) so for example 116.99 becomes 117 not 116. The specific rounding behavior links to [CSS Values & Units 4](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values-4/#combine-integers) but not I am puzzled because that says\n\n> and the result is converted to an <integer> by [rounding to the nearest integer](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values-4/#css-round-to-the-nearest-integer).\n\nha but it also says\n\n> Unless otherwise specified, in the CSS specifications rounding to the nearest integer requires rounding in the direction of +∞ when the fractional portion is exactly 0.5.\n\nwhich is a) no change, for positive numbers it is exactly the same as normal rounding\nb) only affects the case where the fractional part to be rounded is `.50000`. It would not affect `136.425`\n\nSo I think the `rounded towards +∞` is confusing, if people thing it means\"round up always\".\n\n@tabatkins  should Color 4 update to more precise language for that link??",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
